-- WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, DELIBERATELY
-- The naive live-vs-declared diff reports 55 "missing" columns. 35 of those are
-- the SAME column under two names — schema.ts says `ab_test_status`, production
-- has `status`; schema.ts says `yt_status`, production has `yt_pipeline_status`.
-- Adding them would leave production holding both the real column (with data)
-- and a new empty one that the app then reads and writes. No error is raised.
-- That is silent data divergence and it is NOT fixed here. Drift reconciliation
-- is a separate, deliberate piece of work; see the plan document, Part 6.
--
-- The reproducible evidence for the 16-vs-55 split:
--   node scripts/extract-schema-columns.mjs drizzle/schema.ts /tmp/cols.json
--   node scripts/pair-drift-vs-additions.mjs
